body:
`auto` and lambdas are generally disallowed/discouraged in Godot, as per the [contributing docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/contributing/development/cpp_usage_guidelines.html#auto-keyword).

I think here, it would be better to instead introduce a subclass of `VBoxContainer` that contains the necessary information, and then add instances of that subclass to `diag_vbox` instead. So the code here would look something like:
```cpp
for (const EditorLanguage::ScriptError &e : errors) {
    DiagnosticItemRow *new_row = memnew(DiagnosticItemRow);
    new_row->set_error(e);
    diag_vbox->add_child(new_row);
}
for (const EditorLanguage::Warning &w : warnings) {
    DiagnosticItemRow *new_row = memnew(DiagnosticItemRow);
    new_row->set_warning(w);
    diag_vbox->add_child(new_row);
}
```

